claim.claim-text:
(a) at least one vitamin, wherein said vitamin is selected from the group comprising or, alternatively, consisting of: (a-I) at least one vitamin of group B, (a-II) a vitamin C, (a-III) a vitamin D3, (a-IV) a vitamin E, (a-V) a vitamin A and mixtures thereof;
(b) at least one phospholipid, and
(c-i) at least one sucrester or a fatty acid carbohydrate ester.

(a) at least one vitamin, wherein said vitamin is selected from the group comprising or, alternatively, consisting of: (a-I) at least one vitamin of group B, preferably vitamin B12, (a-II) a vitamin C, (a-III) a vitamin D, preferably D3, (a-IV) a vitamin E, (a-V) a vitamin A and mixtures thereof;
(b) at least one phosphatidylcholine or lecithin, preferably sunflower lecithin (E322);
(c-i) a sucrester or a fatty acid carbohydrate ester, preferably a sucrester (E473) comprising from 70% by weight to 90% by weight, with respect to the total weight of the sucrester, of monoesters obtained by esterification of sucrose with one or more fatty acids of plant origin, preferably stearic acid and/or palmitic acid.
(d) a rice starch, preferably pre-gelatinised rice starch.

- (1) preparing said (a) at least one vitamin or mixture of vitamins in the form of powder or granules, to obtain a vitamin of step 1;
- (2) mixing - in the absence of solvent - said vitamin of step 1 with a phospholipid (b), preferably lecithin, and a sucrester (c-i) to obtain a mixture or formulation of step 2;
- (3), optional, mixing said mixture or formulation of step 2 with a starch of plant origin (d), preferably gelatinised or pre-gelatinised, more preferably pre-gelatinised rice starch, to obtain the formulation.
